tasks.brief:
Fix the single bug in /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/inventory.ts. You may edit ONLY that file.

The doc comment says: Takes qty units if that many are left; returns whether it did.

Current reserve (the bug):
```
export function reserve(sku: string, qty: number): boolean {
	const have = stock.get(sku) ?? 0;
	if (have <= qty) { return false; }
	stock.set(sku, have - qty);
	return true;
}
```
The comparison is wrong. `have <= qty` rejects the case where stock equals the requested quantity, so reserve('A1', 3) returns false when A1 has exactly 3. It should succeed whenever have >= qty and fail only when have < qty.

Change the condition to:
```
	if (have < qty) { return false; }
```

Do not change inStock, the stock map, comments, or anything else. Do not edit /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/test/inventory.test.ts or any other file. Do not run npm test.

Fix the single bug in /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/src/checkout.ts. You may edit ONLY that file.

The doc comment says: Reserves every sku (throws 'out of stock <sku>' when one can't be), then returns the cart total.

Current checkout (the bug):
```
export function checkout(cart: Cart, skus: Array<[string, number]>, discountPct: number): number {
	for (const [sku, qty] of skus) {
		if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { continue; }
	}
	return cart.total(discountPct);
}
```
When reserve fails it continues instead of throwing. The test expects assert.throws(() => checkout(c, [['B2', 1]], 0), /out of stock B2/).

Change the failure branch to throw:
```
		if (!reserve(sku, qty)) { throw new Error('out of stock ' + sku); }
```

Do not change the loop, the return, imports, the signature, or comments. Do not edit /tmp/vcmp/w/t2/test/checkout.test.ts or any other file. Do not run npm test.

